/-!
# The actual hexagonal base cover for higher cusp specialization

The original marked base torus is presented by the literal compact dual
hexagon under the shared inverse-quarter-turn lattice coordinate. Its
actual radius-one boundary is homeomorphic to the three-edge theta
graph; the inner region is contractible, the outer region strongly
retracts onto the boundary, and the overlap is an actual annulus.

All maps retain their original quotient and subspace topologies. The
phase-product cover retains the compact fibre phases exactly. Its
overlap inclusions are the actual phase projection and the product of
the phase identity with the genuine circle-to-theta attaching map.
The latter has proved zero first homology, and singular Mayer–Vietoris
supplies actual connecting lifts of the phase-projection kernel.

No CW presentation, boundary identification, deformation retraction,
attaching-map homology formula, or connecting surjectivity is assumed.
-/
